# Main's card — the claim loop (v3, 2026-09-03)

One claim (`CLAIM.md`), one loop (`WORKFLOW.md`). Main never reasons about the science, never summarises a report, never types a number. Each turn Main does exactly one thing: run `python3 .research/stage.py` and execute the one `step.py` action it prints per chain (or wait). Nothing else is Main's to decide.

## The stages (stage.py decides from files)
| Stage | Trigger | Main runs | Who |
|---|---|---|---|
| A frame | no `CLAIM.md` | `bundle.py A` → `frame.workflow.js` | scientist (Fable) |
| R review | claim not accepted / edited; or the mechanism map has no open source | **owner**: `stage.py accept` (refuses a `keep_gain` below the Lehr MDE when `seed_sd` is set); read `.research/mechanism-map.json` | human |
| M mechanism | accepted, no `mechanism-map.json` for this claim text; or an eligible source has no `critique` | `step.py mechanism` → `mechanism.workflow.js` → `step.py mechanism --finish <out>`; then **Slot 1**: `step.py critique sources` → `Workflow(critique)` → `step.py critique --finish sources <out>` (three families, script aggregates: majority anchored drop, mean rank, `contested`) | Opus 5 (B, M) · K3 (C) · Grok (recipe, precedent) · sol + K3 + GLM (panel) |
| C loop | map has open sources, no KEEP-complete ladder, no stop | per chain, one of: `step.py propose <chain> [--rung R]` → Workflow(spec) → `step.py propose --finish <Q>` (gate) → **Slot 2** on a mechanism spec: `step.py critique spec <Q>` → Workflow(critique) → `step.py critique --finish spec <Q> <out>` (advance → `propose --finish` again → card; revise → `propose --retry` once; abandon → queued, source patience +1) → `step.py build <Q>` → Workflow(build) → `step.py build --finish <Q> <out>` → wait → `step.py record <Q>` | Opus 5 · sol + K3 + GLM (panel) · GLM (builder) · Grok plugin (diff) |
| P pivot | no improvement 24 h / 24 search GPU-h / every map source exhausted; or the ladder is complete but fewer than `keep_networks` networks reach the band | `bundle.py pivot` → `pivot.workflow.js` → `step.py pivot --finish <out>` → **owner** picks an exit: (a) `stage.py ship --why "…"` (needs the saved pivot verdict + a valid baseline record; writes `.research/SHIP-INCUMBENT`, stage D then runs with the incumbent as the main-table row and every candidate as a negative result) · (b) edit CLAIM.md and re-accept · (c) `step.py mechanism` with the pivot's associations | explorer (K3) |
| D write | one KEEP (3 seeds, CI95 > 0) and the support ladder done (other networks, ablation), one rung at a time | `bundle.py write` → `write.workflow.js` → `gate.py numbers` → latexmk | writer (GLM), Fable, Grok |
| STOP | `.research/IDENTITY-MISMATCH` exists; or three consecutive infrastructure queues within 2 h (`.research/INFRA-STOP`) | fix the model pin / the proxy, re-probe, delete the marker | human |
| DONE | `.research/DONE` exists (deliverables gate passed) | nothing | — |

Workflows do semantic fan-out only and receive everything inline in `args` (a JSON string; every script parses it defensively). Deterministic steps run in `step.py` between workflow calls. Workflows never call each other. When `step.py` says "save the returned JSON to <path>", write the workflow's result there verbatim with Write (or pass the runtime's "full result in <path>" file), then run the `--finish` it names. A workflow that returns `null`/`error` is an infrastructure failure: every `--finish` refuses to gate it, counts it on disk, and prints the retry; the third in a row within 2 h stops the loop.

## Unattended run
`/goal "python3 .research/stage.py prints STAGE D or STAGE P; print stage.py board and stage.py map every turn; or stop after 60 turns"`. While a `research-*.service` is running, wait (Monitor on `systemctl --user is-active research-<run>.service`, or ScheduleWakeup ≥ 20 min); `stage.py` shows the run's progress (fraction, dev_gain) each turn. First live run: alpha only; open beta after alpha's first record.

## Rules
1. `CLAIM.md` is edited by the owner only; `stage.py accept` records its sha; `gate.py card` refuses while the sha differs; the write-guard hook denies any lane that touches loop state.
2. Ideas come from the mechanism map (A → failure mode B grounded in `.research/anomalies.md` → abstract mechanism M → source domain C with a recipe and a disanalogy), never from a lane's free text. A source with no procedure or with a precedent in A is dropped by script.
3. The kill test is the whole build; one candidate per chain at a time. Token only after `gate.py monitor` approved the current diff: ONE external lens (the Grok plugin via the `reviewer` forwarder, `review --json`; critical/high findings block; unavailable = infrastructure, retried, never a verdict) plus script facts (every spec step's file is in the intent-to-add diff, no gitlink/symlink, `eval_entry` untouched). The GLM monitor lane was retired 2026-09-04 (stalled on large diffs). The token names the card sha AND the diff sha; the launcher recomputes the diff sha and refuses if the worktree changed after review.
4. Cut losses by script: the unit runs a SMOKE phase first (canary), then the watchdog kills a run whose dev_gain is below the early-stop line at 25% / 50% of the schedule (exit 4 = a recorded early kill) or that stalls (exit 5 = infrastructure). Same source twice without a new best → source exhausted; next candidate must change source.
5. Only a record refutes: `render_record.py` + `gate.py record` (unit exit 0 or 4, exit 0 needs fraction ≥ 0.95, seed mtimes inside a launcher window, `blockers.json` and `progress.json` present and inside the window, no `high` blocker unless `bundle.py waive <Q> "<why>"` logged it, canary bar from the frozen spec, `clean_cost`, metric = claim metric). `step.py record` writes the verdict into the record (`gate_pass`); a refused record is queued and never counts (not for best, kill line, map, KEEP). Never edit `records/`, `ledger.jsonl`, `notebook.json`, `mechanism-map.json`, `cards/` by hand.
6. No GPU work outside `GPU=<n> [SEEDS=…] bin/run_protected.sh <run> <card> <mem>G <cmd>`; `step.py` is the only caller.
7. A workflow that returns nothing is an infrastructure failure, not a verdict: `bundle.py queue <Q> "<what>"`, move on. One fix round per gate, then queue. Never re-run a workflow by hand with a changed prompt.
8. Generalisation only after one model keeps: the support ladder (R1 full schedule on the kept network = the headline, then other networks, ablation) runs one rung at a time as ordinary candidates with `phase: support` (cap `support_gpu_h_cap`, default 40; exempt from the dedup gate); support and baseline runs never count against the search budget. The kill test and its confirm seeds are a screen: the paper's main table takes only `role: headline` records.
9. One writer: if the session-start hook printed READ-ONLY, do not write cards, tokens, or launch.
10. Numbers enter `paper/merged/` only from `records/`, each line with `% src: <record>`; `gate.py numbers` checks it and the retracted-number blacklist.

## Commands
- `python3 .research/stage.py` · `stage.py board` · `stage.py map` · `stage.py accept [--by X --why "…"]` (owner; refuses without `seed_sd`/`a_terms`, below the MDE, or below the last accepted `keep_gain`; logged to `ledger.jsonl`)
- `python3 .research/step.py {mechanism [--finish <out>] | critique sources | critique spec <Q> | critique --finish sources <out> | critique --finish spec <Q> <out> | propose <chain> [--rung R] [--retry] | propose --finish <Q> [<out>] | build <Q> [--fix] | build --finish <Q> <out> | record <Q> | write --finish <out> | pivot --finish <out> | status <Q>}`
- `python3 .research/bundle.py {A|M|mechanism-finish <out>|spec --chain X [--rung R] [--retry]|card <spec_path>|build <Q> [--fix]|token <Q>|notebook <Q>|write|pivot|queue <Q> "<text>"}`
- `python3 .research/gate.py {spec <Q> | card <card_path> | freeze <card_path> | cardsha <card> | monitor <Q> <out.json> | diffsha <wt> | record <record_path> <card_path> | numbers <tex…> | deliverables}` · `bundle.py waive <Q> "<why>"` (owner)
- Tests: `python3 -m pytest .research/tests -q` · `bash .research/tests/test_launcher.sh` (needs the LOCK)

## Environment and gotchas
- The experiment repo (`repo_root` in GOAL.md) must have a `research-trunk` branch; candidates run in `git worktree`s at `/tmp/wt-<Q>` on branches `exp/<Q>`; results live under the worktree (`/tmp/wt-<Q>/results/<run>/`).
- Pin the model of every lane in `.claude/agents/*.md`; the identity probe stops the loop on a silent substitution (`.research/IDENTITY-MISMATCH`).
- Hooks (plugin): session lock, launch gate, dispatch guard, write guard, identity probe. `Workflow(<name>)` for the six workflows is allowed by `init`.
- Builder result contract (in every build bundle): `$RESULTS_DIR/seed_$SEED.json`, `$RESULTS_DIR/blockers.json`, and `$RESULTS_DIR/progress.json` rewritten at every eval checkpoint (`fraction`, `dev_gain`, `clean_dev_cost`, `loss`).
- Optional CLAIM fields the scripts read: `a_terms`, `early_stop: {at, min_gain, stall_min}`, `support_ladder: [{kind, value}]`, `held_out_terms`, `a_terms` (required: the precedent search), `seed_sd` (required: accept checks `keep_gain` ≥ 2.8·sd·√(2/n); also the hill-climb margin), `eval_entry` (every `kill_cmd` must call it; no spec step or diff may touch it), `support_gpu_h_cap`, `stop_dry_runs` (default 4 completed candidates without a new best), chain `mode: baseline` (its records are the comparator, never a candidate). The claim sentence names no method: candidates come from the mechanism map, the chain's `seed_method` is only the incumbent baseline.
- The Grok plugin is found by glob under `~/.claude/plugins/cache/grok/` (`GROK_COMPANION` overrides); a missing or failing plugin is an infrastructure failure (retried), never a verdict.
- The trunk keeps `repos/*` as gitlinks: a worktree has them EMPTY and an edit inside one is one `Subproject commit` line to the diff (unreviewable, refused by the monitor and the launcher). Before any candidate touches model code the owner tracks it as files on `research-trunk`.
- Bash cwd persists between tool calls; use absolute paths.
